            <ArticleTitle>[Coronarography, technique and results (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>24-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angiography is a radiologic special technique with its place in the diagnosis of coronary disease. It demands much equipment and time. Evaluation, particularly in coronary sclerosis, is valuable, since it makes subtile differential diagnosis possible. This in turn is the basis for modern individual therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
